From: acmeplus <acmeplus@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/adreno: add Adreno 710

A7xx gen1 part of the Parrot SoCs (kgsl gen7_3_0, chip id 0x07010000).
Based on the A730 entry with the kgsl differences: no BV clock-gating
registers, 512K GMEM, smaller preemption record.  The crash-state register
dump is skipped: the A730 snapshot lists hang the bus on this GPU.

sunshineinabox: hwcg list and A730 protect list checked against kgsl; 
differences carried over: GBIF client QoS 0x3, no UCHE GMEM range, 
no BV/LPAC APRIV or BV RPTR writes; preemption enabled; speed bins from the
stock gpu-pwrlevel-bins andSH0/MC0/ACV BCMs for GMU bandwidth voting, 
which replaces the A730 HFI bandwidth-table special case.

Co-developed-by: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_catalog.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_catalog.c
@@ -1192,6 +1192,63 @@
 	{}
 };
 
